 "notes": "Stretch 1: p.127 from row 3 ('1. ànet' ḥrà - k χabes') to foot ('māket - f'), then p.128 all 9 rows to 'Àusàr' ('Osiris,'). All plate XIX. Line numerals: '1.' p.127 row 3 start; '2.' p.127 row 5 start; '3.' p.127 row 6 before ànet' (after Ḥeru - χuti); '4.' p.127 row 8 before ànet' (after Àḳert); '5.' p.128 row 1 after Ṭeṭṭu; '6.' p.128 row 3 after àuset-s; '7.' p.128 row 5 after Sutenḥenen; '8.' p.128 row 7 after ḳer; '9.' p.128 row 9 after Neχen. Last numeral on p.128 is 9. Overlines: only over each 'ànet' ḥrà - k' after numerals 1-9, each covering exactly that group (both transliteration words); no other overlines. No square brackets in the sign line; brackets only in English ([lord of], [and of], [thou], [who]). No footnotes on these pages. 'ànet' ḥrà - k' is split as two words (ànet' / ḥrà - k) since Budge prints them as separate groups; gloss 'Homage to thee' put on ànet'. Several signs on p.127-128 have no exact Gardiner code (lamp in χabes, Seker bark, sign in ḳer, head in atet) — see unsure."
